# Brief

Filled by `intake` from what was actually asked. Quote the requester where it matters; mark anything inferred as **(inferred)** so it can be corrected.

## The problem, without a solution in it

"Users can't tell which plan they're on" is a problem. "Redesign the plan page" is a solution wearing a problem's clothes. [[ASK: the problem in the requester's words]]

## Who is in the middle of this

A real person mid-task, not a persona with a stock photo: what they are trying to get done, and what gets in the way.

## Hard constraints

Only what genuinely can't move (deadline, platform, regulation, budget band). Preferences go under principles.

## Principles

2–4 statements that can each reject an idea. "Simple and delightful" rejects nothing; "a first-time user finishes without help text" rejects plenty.

## Already committed

Decisions made before work starts (also logged in `docs/decisions.md`).

## Links

Shared-drive folder, source files, meeting notes. Linked, not copied in.
